{"assets":[],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"467","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"E. Alex and Complicated Task"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"2 seconds"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"After you have read all the problems, probably, you think Alex is genius person. That's true! One day he came up with the following task."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Given a sequence of integer numbers "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"a1, a2, ..., an"},{"kind":"text","text":". You are to find a longest sequence "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"b1, b2, ..., b4m"},{"kind":"text","text":", that satisfies the following conditions:"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":false},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"math_inline","text":"b4k + 1 = b4k + 3"},{"kind":"text","text":" for all valid integer "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"k"},{"kind":"text","text":"; "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"math_inline","text":"b4k + 2 = b4k + 4"},{"kind":"text","text":" for all valid integer "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"k"},{"kind":"text","text":"; "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" sequence "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"b"},{"kind":"text","text":" is subsequence of "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"a"},{"kind":"text","text":" (not necessarily contiguous subsequence). "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"And finally... Alex had given this complicated task to George, and George gave it to you. Help George to cope with the task."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line contains a single integer "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"(1 ≤ n ≤ 5·105)"},{"kind":"text","text":". The next line contains "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":" integers "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"a1, a2, ..., an"},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"(1 ≤ ai ≤ 109)"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the first line print a single integer "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"4m"},{"kind":"text","text":" — the maximal possible length of required sequence "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"b"},{"kind":"text","text":". In the second line print "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"4m"},{"kind":"text","text":" integers "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"b1, b2, ..., b4m"},{"kind":"text","text":", that is required sequence."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"If there are multiple optimal answers you may print any of them."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Examples"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"4\n3 5 3 5\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"4\n3 5 3 5\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"